      "text": "The failure comes from the `s` gate. The basis `{h, t, cx, id}` is universal, but Qiskit's equivalence library has no rule that rewrites `s` into those gates. Since S = T·T exactly, I replace the `s` gate with two `t` gates, which keeps the same circuit and uses only the allowed gates.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit.circuit import QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit import transpile\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(2)\nqc.h(0)\n# FIX: qc.s(0) used a gate with no translation rule into basis {h, t, cx, id} -> replaced with two t gates, because T·T = S exactly so the circuit is unchanged and uses only basis gates\nqc.t(0)\nqc.t(0)\nqc.cx(0, 1)\n\nbasis_gates = [\"h\", \"t\", \"cx\", \"id\"]\nqc_transpiled = transpile(qc, basis_gates=basis_gates)\n```",
